<header><p class="st-kicker">crusader state · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Thessalonica</h1><p class="st-meta">1204 CE – 1224 CE · capital Thessalonica</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Crusader kingdom created for Boniface of Montferrat after the Fourth Crusade, which lasted only twenty years before falling to Epirus.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boniface-i-marquis-of-montferrat">Boniface of Montferrat</a>, leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a>, lost the election for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> emperor in 1204 but received <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaloniki">Thessalonica</a> and much of Macedonia and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaly">Thessaly</a>. He married Margaret of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, widow of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isaac-ii-angelos">Isaac II</a>, and invaded central and southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, granting fiefs such as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-athens">Duchy of Athens</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/marquisate-of-bodonitsa">Marquisate of Bodonitsa</a> to his followers.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kingdom was ruled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> nobles from northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> over a Greek population, under nominal homage to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/latin-empire">Latin Empire</a>. A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> archbishop replaced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> metropolitan. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boniface-i-marquis-of-montferrat">Boniface</a> was killed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgarians">Bulgarians</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaloyan-of-bulgaria">Kaloyan</a> in 1207, leaving his infant son Demetrius under a regency; the Lombard barons' revolt of 1208-1209 was suppressed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-of-flanders">Emperor Henry</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Weakened by internal divisions and Bulgarian attacks, the kingdom was gradually conquered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodore-komnenos-doukas">Theodore Komnenos Doukas</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epirus">Epirus</a>, who took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaloniki">Thessalonica</a> itself in 1224 and founded the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/empire-of-thessalonica">Empire of Thessalonica</a>. The title survived among Western claimants.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-thessalonica.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Thessalonica" width="320" height="169"><figcaption>Image: LatinEmpire · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LatinEmpire2.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1204 CE – 1224 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>crusader state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Thessalonica</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Boniface of Montferrat, Demetrius of Montferrat</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity (rulers), Eastern Orthodox Christianity (population)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old French, Italian, Medieval Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a>, <a href="/countries/north-macedonia">North Macedonia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Latin Kingdom of Thessalonica</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1214&amp;focus=kingdom-of-thessalonica" aria-label="Kingdom of Thessalonica on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5243 726 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Thessalonica lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5563 982L5709 970M5563 982L5519 1030M5563 982L5580 1057M5563 982L5561 1043M5563 982L5556 1051"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5709 970h0M5519 1030h0M5580 1057h0M5561 10